# Certificates a PEC receipt's S/MIME signature must lead to (pec.rs).
#
# Where they come from: AgID keeps the list of accredited PEC providers
# (https://www.agid.gov.it/it/piattaforme/posta-elettronica-certificata)
# and, in the providers' index (IGPEC), the certificate each provider signs
# its receipts with. The index itself is open only to the providers, so the
# certificates have to be taken from the providers' own receipts or from
# AgID on request, and checked against the published list before they go
# in here. The CAs in the Italian trusted list (TSL-IT,
# https://eidas.agid.gov.it/TL/TSL-IT.xml) are not enough on their own:
# they also certify people, whose signatures must not pass for a
# provider's.
#
# How it is updated: add each provider's certificate (or the CA that
# issued it, if that CA certifies nothing else) as a PEM block below, with
# a comment naming the provider and the date it was checked; remove a
# provider when AgID lists it as ceased.
#
# Until a certificate is here, every receipt shows as unverified in the
# Vault: it is never presented as proof.
